      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RIPP (10) is a reliable gelding who continues to race well having added to a string of top-four results when coming from a similar barrier to finish 4.5m behind race rival GLITTER AINT GOLD last week. Starts inside that rival tonight and that gives him the chance to turn the tables. GLITTER AINT GOLD (11) draws much wider than when he won the Vic Frost FFA last time out but that was his second Listed success in his last three outings here so is clearly in good form. If things go his way he could deliver again. SMOKEN ACE NZ (9) draws wider than in his resuming fifth behind GLITTER AINT GOLD but owns a good second-up record so can progress. PICCADILLY PETE NZ (3) looks an each way hope having clocked in fourth from this barrier last week after coming from wider to place in the Vic Frost. HUTA NZ (7) draws better than last start and has claims off a win from a similar barrier to this here prior.",
